<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="64.2" level="1">Wills, Trusts, and Fiduciaries</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="IV" level="2">Fiduciaries and Guardians</unit>
		<unit label="part" identifier="B" level="3">Powers of Attorney</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="16" level="4">Uniform Power of Attorney Act</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="1" level="5">General Provisions</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>64.2-1611</section_number>
	<catch_line>Agent's acceptance</catch_line>
	<text>
		Except as otherwise provided in the power of attorney, a person accepts appointment as an agent under a power of attorney by exercising authority or performing duties as an agent or by any other assertion or conduct indicating acceptance.
	</text>
	<history>2010, cc. 455, 632, § 26-84; 2012, c. 614.</history>
</law>
